The Pythagorean theorem must hold: a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> = c<sup>2</sup>, where c is the hypotenuse For a right-angled triangle.
a) {3, 4, 6}
=> 3<sup>2</sup> + 4<sup>2</sup> = 9 + 16 = 25 ≠ 6<sup>2</sup>
=> 25 ≠ 36
b) {8, 15, 16}
=> 8<sup>2</sup> + 15<sup>2</sup> = 64 + 225 = 289 ≠ 16<sup>2</sup>
=> 289 ≠ 256
c) {5, 10, 12}
=> 5<sup>2</sup> + 10<sup>2</sup> = 25 + 100 = 125 ≠ 12<sup>2</sup>
=> 125 ≠ 144
d) {5, 12, 13}
=> 5<sup>2</sup> + 12<sup>2</sup> = 25 + 144 = 169 = 13<sup>2</sup>
=> 169 = 169
